  "current front (NBLK 4 x BLK 8; block credit covers in-flight) streams K at ~0.45 sector/HBM edge while the static QK pass consumes 1 sector/core edge/PC (1.23x the HBM rate): at T=8192 the return ring would need 160 sectors vs DEPTH 8 -> hold faults; the writer r4 / return r2 holds can NOT be released on the current sizes",
  "sized boundary (front NBLK 12, return ring DEPTH 64) closes all contexts: ring peak 48 at T=8192 (= 256 x (1 - 833.3/1024) frequency prefill), K fetch 315 core edges, QK starts 111 core edges after the PC prefetch start; the prefetch is issued before the attention request in the static schedule -> 0 added cycles",
  "the token own K row (t = T-1) is the LAST K read of its PC: its HBM write must commit before that RD (~200 core edges after QK start)",
  "per-PC HBM busy 514 of 5402 HBM edges per layer at T=8192: bandwidth is not the limit; refresh calendar and V per-PC order are open inputs"
 ],
